blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:91:	Fix $\mathsf{ldparams} = (q,m,d,k)$ as in Definition~\ref{def:ld-game}, let $L = \{L_t\}_{t \in \mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}}}$ be the family of Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}, and let $G^{\mathrm{ld}}$ be the graph on $\mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}}$ all of whose unordered pairs, self-loops included, are edges. Then the question distribution of $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{ld}}$ is the $(\mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}}, G^{\mathrm{ld}})$-typed conditionally linear distribution $\mu^{G^{\mathrm{ld}}}_{L,\,L}$ of Definition~\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}. The linked declaration proves the distribution identity: the question distribution of $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{ld}}$ equals the distribution that the construction of Definition~\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from the pair $(L, L)$ and the graph $G^{\mathrm{ld}}$, a construction that is available for an arbitrary family of maps. It does not prove that $L$ is a $\mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}}$-typed family of conditionally linear functions of one common level, which is what makes the right-hand side a typed conditionally linear distribution in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}: Lemmas~\ref{lem:ld-aline-level} and~\ref{lem:ld-dline-level} give the levels of $L_{\mathsf{ALine}}$ and $L_{\mathsf{DLine}}$, while the level of $L_{\mathsf{Point}}$ and the passage of the three maps to a common level are not formalized. That family assertion is open and is tracked as issue~\#180, so the statement and the proof below carry no completion mark.
